{"kind":"project","variants":[{"paths":["\/tutorials\/loomcore\/expressionsandservices"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"categoryPathComponent":"LoomCore","category":"LoomCore","title":"Expressions and services","role":"project"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/$volume","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/Expressions-and-services"]],"reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore","modules":[{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/GettingStarted","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/GettingStarted#Open-a-database"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/GettingStarted#Define-a-schema"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/GettingStarted#Insert-rows-safely"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/GettingStarted#Query-with-a-stepper"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/GettingStarted#Group-writes-in-a-transaction"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/GettingStarted#Check-Your-Understanding"}]}],"reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/Getting-started"},{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/ExpressionsAndServices","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/ExpressionsAndServices#Configure-the-database-for-production"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/ExpressionsAndServices#Model-rows-with-Codable"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/ExpressionsAndServices#Build-queries-with-ColumnExpression"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/ExpressionsAndServices#React-to-commits-with-services"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/ExpressionsAndServices#Check-Your-Understanding"}]}],"reference":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/Expressions-and-services"}]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/ExpressionsAndServices"},"sections":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Build a small task tracker that uses ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ColumnExpression","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and the operator DSL for type-checked queries, stores per-task metadata as JSON via ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONBindable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", tunes SQLite for production with PRAGMA, and uses ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to invalidate an in-process cache on commit.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"By the end you will know how to combine expressions for non-trivial WHERE clauses, when to reach for ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ColumnExpression","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" versus raw SQL, and how to wire long-lived state to transaction lifecycle events.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"chapter":"Expressions and services","title":"Expressions and services","estimatedTimeInMinutes":25,"kind":"hero"},{"tasks":[{"stepsSection":[{"caption":[],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Open a file-backed database. Switch to WAL mode for concurrent reads, set ","type":"text"},{"code":"synchronous = NORMAL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (a safe default in WAL), and enable foreign-key enforcement.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","media":null,"code":"ex-01-setup.swift","runtimePreview":null},{"runtimePreview":null,"code":"ex-02-schema.swift","caption":[],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create three related tables. Foreign keys give us the integrity guarantees we need; storing freeform metadata as JSON keeps the schema small."}]}],"type":"step","media":null}],"contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default SQLite settings favour single-writer use. For an app with concurrent reads — even in a single process — WAL mode plus foreign-key enforcement is a better baseline. LoomCore exposes the relevant PRAGMAs as typed accessors so you do not need to remember their string forms."}]}]}],"anchor":"Configure-the-database-for-production","title":"Configure the database for production"},{"stepsSection":[{"caption":[],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Define a "},{"code":"TaskMetadata","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value that holds a few optional fields. Conforming to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Bindable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is enough; LoomCore picks up the JSON encoder automatically via the protocol’s default implementation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","media":null,"code":"ex-03-metadata.swift","runtimePreview":null},{"caption":[],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Define ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Category","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" models. Note that ","type":"text"},{"code":"Category.id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — LoomCore stores it as a 16-byte BLOB.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","media":null,"code":"ex-04-models.swift","runtimePreview":null},{"media":null,"code":"ex-05-insert.swift","runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Insert a row. The interpolated ","type":"text"},{"code":"metadata","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is JSON-encoded by its "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONBindable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" conformance and bound as a parameter — there is no manual ","type":"text"},{"code":"JSONEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call. The write is wrapped in "},{"code":"db.transaction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so that the commit notifies the services we build at the end of this tutorial."}]}],"caption":[],"type":"step"}],"contentSection":[{"kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" types become "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Bindable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" by conforming to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONBindable"},{"type":"text","text":". Their values are JSON-encoded and stored as TEXT — precisely so SQLite’s JSON functions ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"json_extract"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"->","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"->>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") can query into them directly when you need to.","type":"text"}]}],"mediaPosition":"trailing"}],"anchor":"Model-rows-with-Codable","title":"Model rows with Codable"},{"stepsSection":[{"code":"ex-06-columns.swift","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare the columns you will query against. A static struct keeps them in one place — and gives autocomplete.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"step","runtimePreview":null,"caption":[],"media":null},{"code":"ex-07-query.swift","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Find all open tasks in a category. The expression ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tasks.categoryID == categoryID && tasks.completedAt.isNull()"},{"type":"text","text":" is built in Swift, then interpolated into the SQL — the compiler ensures "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"categoryID"},{"text":" is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UUID"},{"type":"text","text":", not a "},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"step","runtimePreview":null,"caption":[],"media":null},{"caption":[],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use an aggregate. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"groupConcat"},{"type":"text","text":" joins values across rows into a single string; the result type is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String?"},{"type":"text","text":" because SQL "},{"code":"GROUP_CONCAT","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" returns NULL for an empty group."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","media":null,"code":"ex-08-aggregate.swift","runtimePreview":null},{"code":"ex-09-in.swift","runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"code":"IN","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with a set of UUIDs. An empty array is renders as an always-false expression rather than invalid SQL — so you do not have to special-case “the user picked no categories”.","type":"text"}]}],"media":null,"caption":[]}],"contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ColumnExpression","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is the typed, properly-quoted way to refer to a column in expression-DSL code. Combined with operator overloads on ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", you can write ","type":"text"},{"code":"WHERE","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" clauses in Swift that the compiler checks for type compatibility.","type":"text"}]}]}],"anchor":"Build-queries-with-ColumnExpression","title":"Build queries with ColumnExpression"},{"title":"React to commits with services","contentSection":[{"kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is a long-lived helper that receives transaction lifecycle callbacks. The classic use case is invalidating a cache when the data behind it changes. Services are singletons per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Database"},{"type":"text","text":" and per type, so you do not have to manage their lifetime manually."}]}],"mediaPosition":"trailing"}],"anchor":"React-to-commits-with-services","stepsSection":[{"code":"ex-10-cache.swift","runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Define a small in-process cache for category counts. It will be invalidated on every commit.","type":"text"}]}],"media":null,"caption":[]},{"caption":[],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the cache to a service. "},{"code":"transactionDidCommit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called after every committed outermost transaction; ","type":"text"},{"code":"transactionDidRollback","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called on rollback. Nested (savepoint) scopes fire no callbacks — only the physical transaction does. You can tighten this up by tracking which tables changed if you need finer-grained invalidation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","media":null,"code":"ex-11-service.swift","runtimePreview":null},{"caption":[],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the cache from your store. Only writes wrapped in an outermost "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.transaction { db in … }"},{"type":"text","text":" that commits notify the service — a bare "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"exec"},{"type":"text","text":" outside a transaction fires no callbacks. That is why "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add"},{"type":"text","text":" wraps its INSERT in a transaction: every committed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add"},{"type":"text","text":" invalidates the cache, and the next read recomputes it."}]}],"type":"step","media":null,"code":"ex-12-cached-query.swift","runtimePreview":null}]}],"kind":"tasks"},{"assessments":[{"content":[],"type":"multiple-choice","title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Why is ","type":"text"},{"code":"ColumnExpression","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" preferable to interpolating a column name in ","type":"text"},{"code":".raw","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" mode?","type":"text"}]}],"choices":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It always renders quoted identifiers and rejects empty\/NUL names."}]}],"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Quoting makes reserved words and identifiers with spaces safe; validation closes off a class of programmer errors."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is faster."}]}],"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Speed is not the reason. Both produce the same SQL fragment."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It binds the column name as a parameter."}]}],"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Column names cannot be parameters in SQLite. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ColumnExpression"},{"type":"text","text":" renders them as literal SQL — but quoted and validated."}]}]}]},{"content":[],"type":"multiple-choice","title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"What is the return type of ","type":"text"},{"code":"ColumnExpression<String>(\"body\").groupConcat()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"?","type":"text"}]}],"choices":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GroupConcat"},{"type":"text","text":" whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExpressionValue"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String?"}]}],"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GROUP_CONCAT"},{"type":"text","text":" returns NULL for empty groups, so the typealias is optional."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GroupConcat"},{"type":"text","text":" whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExpressionValue"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"}]}],"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That would lose the empty-group case — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GROUP_CONCAT"},{"type":"text","text":" is nullable."}]}]}]},{"content":[],"type":"multiple-choice","title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When does ","type":"text"},{"code":"transactionDidCommit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fire on a service?","type":"text"}]}],"choices":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After every outermost transaction opened via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.transaction { db in … }"},{"type":"text","text":" that commits successfully."}]}],"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Implicit per-statement transactions — a bare "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"exec"},{"type":"text","text":" outside a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transaction"},{"type":"text","text":" block — and nested (savepoint) scopes do not fire service callbacks."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"exec"},{"type":"text","text":" call."}]}],"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only outermost "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transaction { db in … }"},{"type":"text","text":" blocks notify services."}]}]}]}],"anchor":"Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessments"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://LoomCore/tutorials/LoomCore/GettingStarted#Define-a-schema":{"type":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol","title":"Define a schema","abstract":[{"text":"Build a small notes store: open a database, create a schema, insert rows safely, run queries, and group writes in a transaction. By the end you will have a working command-line app that exercises the core LoomCore API.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/loomcore\/gettingstarted#Define-a-schema","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/GettingStarted#Define-a-schema","kind":"section"},"doc://LoomCore/tutorials/LoomCore/Expressions-and-services":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/tutorials\/loomcore\/expressions-and-services","title":"Expressions and services","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/Expressions-and-services","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://LoomCore/tutorials/LoomCore/GettingStarted#Check-Your-Understanding":{"title":"Check Your Understanding","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/GettingStarted#Check-Your-Understanding","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Check Your Understanding"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/loomcore\/gettingstarted#Check-Your-Understanding"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/JSONBindable":{"kind":"symbol","title":"JSONBindable","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Opt-in JSON-as-","type":"text"},{"code":"TEXT","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" storage for ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" types.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONBindable","url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/jsonbindable","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"JSONBindable","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"JSONBindable"}]},"doc://LoomCore/tutorials/LoomCore/GettingStarted#Open-a-database":{"type":"section","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a small notes store: open a database, create a schema, insert rows safely, run queries, and group writes in a transaction. By the end you will have a working command-line app that exercises the core LoomCore API."}],"url":"\/tutorials\/loomcore\/gettingstarted#Open-a-database","title":"Open a database","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/GettingStarted#Open-a-database","kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"doc://LoomCore/tutorials/LoomCore/ExpressionsAndServices#Check-Your-Understanding":{"titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Check Your Understanding","type":"text"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/loomcore\/expressionsandservices#Check-Your-Understanding","title":"Check Your Understanding","type":"link","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/ExpressionsAndServices#Check-Your-Understanding"},"doc://LoomCore/tutorials/LoomCore/ExpressionsAndServices#Build-queries-with-ColumnExpression":{"type":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol","title":"Build queries with ColumnExpression","abstract":[{"text":"Build a small task tracker that uses ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ColumnExpression","type":"reference"},{"text":" and the operator DSL for type-checked queries, stores per-task metadata as JSON via ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONBindable","type":"reference"},{"text":", tunes SQLite for production with PRAGMA, and uses ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service","type":"reference"},{"text":" to invalidate an in-process cache on commit.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/loomcore\/expressionsandservices#Build-queries-with-ColumnExpression","kind":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/ExpressionsAndServices#Build-queries-with-ColumnExpression"},"ex-11-service.swift":{"syntax":"swift","type":"file","fileName":"TaskStore+Cache.swift","content":["import Foundation","import LoomCore","","@DatabaseActor","final class CategoryCountsCache {","    private var counts: [UUID: Int] = [:]","","    func count(for categoryID: UUID, computing: () async throws -> Int) async rethrows -> Int {","        if let cached = counts[categoryID] {","            return cached","        }","        let value = try await computing()","        counts[categoryID] = value","        return value","    }","","    func invalidate() {","        counts.removeAll()","    }","}","","@DatabaseActor","final class CategoryCountsService: Database.Service {","    let cache = CategoryCountsCache()","","    override func transactionDidCommit() {","        cache.invalidate()","    }","","    override func transactionDidRollback() {","        \/\/ No-op: the cache only mirrors committed state, so a rolled-back","        \/\/ transaction did not change anything we could be caching.","    }","}"],"fileType":"swift","highlights":[{"line":21},{"line":22},{"line":23},{"line":24},{"line":25},{"line":26},{"line":27},{"line":28},{"line":29},{"line":30},{"line":31},{"line":32},{"line":33},{"line":34}],"identifier":"ex-11-service.swift"},"doc://LoomCore/tutorials/LoomCore/ExpressionsAndServices#Configure-the-database-for-production":{"type":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol","title":"Configure the database for production","abstract":[{"text":"Build a small task tracker that uses ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ColumnExpression"},{"text":" and the operator DSL for type-checked queries, stores per-task metadata as JSON via ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONBindable"},{"text":", tunes SQLite for production with PRAGMA, and uses ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service"},{"text":" to invalidate an in-process cache on commit.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/loomcore\/expressionsandservices#Configure-the-database-for-production","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/ExpressionsAndServices#Configure-the-database-for-production","kind":"section"},"ex-12-cached-query.swift":{"syntax":"swift","type":"file","fileName":"TaskStore.swift","content":["import Foundation","import LoomCore","","struct TaskStore {","    let db: Database","","    @DatabaseActor","    func add(_ task: TaskRow) async throws {","        try await db.transaction { db in","            try await db.exec(","                \"\"\"","                INSERT INTO tasks (id, category_id, title, completed_at, metadata)","                VALUES (\\(task.id), \\(task.categoryID), \\(task.title), \\(task.completedAt), \\(task.metadata))","                \"\"\"","            )","        }","    }","}","","extension TaskStore {","    @DatabaseActor","    func openTasks(in categoryID: UUID) async throws -> [TaskRow] {","        let predicate =","            TaskColumns.categoryID == categoryID","            && TaskColumns.completedAt.isNull()","","        return try await db.query(","            \"\"\"","            SELECT id, category_id, title, completed_at, metadata","            FROM tasks","            WHERE \\(predicate)","            ORDER BY id","            \"\"\",","            stepper: { stmt, index, _ in","                TaskRow(","                    id: try Int.column(of: stmt, at: &index),","                    categoryID: try UUID.column(of: stmt, at: &index),","                    title: try String.column(of: stmt, at: &index),","                    completedAt: try Date?.column(of: stmt, at: &index),","                    metadata: try TaskMetadata?.column(of: stmt, at: &index)","                )","            }","        )","    }","}","","extension TaskStore {","    @DatabaseActor","    func openTitles(for categoryID: UUID) async throws -> [String] {","        \/\/ GROUP_CONCAT returns a single comma-separated row, or NULL for an empty group.","        let titles = TaskColumns.title.groupConcat(separator: \", \")","        let predicate =","            TaskColumns.categoryID == categoryID","            && TaskColumns.completedAt.isNull()","","        let row = try await db.query(","            \"SELECT \\(titles) FROM tasks WHERE \\(predicate)\",","            stepper: { stmt, _ in try String?.column(of: stmt, at: 0) }","        ).first","","        return (row ?? nil)?.components(separatedBy: \", \") ?? []","    }","}","","extension TaskStore {","    @DatabaseActor","    func tasks(inAnyOf categoryIDs: [UUID]) async throws -> [TaskRow] {","        \/\/ An empty array renders as `( \"tasks\".\"category_id\" IN (NULL) AND 0 )`,","        \/\/ which is an always-false predicate — no special-casing needed.","        let predicate = TaskColumns.categoryID.in(array: categoryIDs)","","        return try await db.query(","            \"\"\"","            SELECT id, category_id, title, completed_at, metadata","            FROM tasks","            WHERE \\(predicate)","            ORDER BY id","            \"\"\",","            stepper: { stmt, index, _ in","                TaskRow(","                    id: try Int.column(of: stmt, at: &index),","                    categoryID: try UUID.column(of: stmt, at: &index),","                    title: try String.column(of: stmt, at: &index),","                    completedAt: try Date?.column(of: stmt, at: &index),","                    metadata: try TaskMetadata?.column(of: stmt, at: &index)","                )","            }","        )","    }","}","","extension TaskStore {","    @DatabaseActor","    func openCount(for categoryID: UUID) async throws -> Int {","        let service = db.getService(CategoryCountsService.self)","","        return try await service.cache.count(for: categoryID) {","            let predicate =","                TaskColumns.categoryID == categoryID","                && TaskColumns.completedAt.isNull()","","            let rows = try await db.query(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM tasks WHERE \\(predicate)\") { stmt, _ in","                try Int.column(of: stmt, at: 0)","            }","            return rows.first ?? 0","        }","    }","}"],"fileType":"swift","highlights":[{"line":91},{"line":92},{"line":93},{"line":94},{"line":95},{"line":96},{"line":97},{"line":98},{"line":99},{"line":100},{"line":101},{"line":102},{"line":103},{"line":104},{"line":105},{"line":106},{"line":107},{"line":108}],"identifier":"ex-12-cached-query.swift"},"doc://LoomCore/tutorials/LoomCore/GettingStarted#Group-writes-in-a-transaction":{"type":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol","title":"Group writes in a transaction","abstract":[{"text":"Build a small notes store: open a database, create a schema, insert rows safely, run queries, and group writes in a transaction. By the end you will have a working command-line app that exercises the core LoomCore API.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/loomcore\/gettingstarted#Group-writes-in-a-transaction","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/GettingStarted#Group-writes-in-a-transaction","kind":"section"},"doc://LoomCore/tutorials/LoomCore/GettingStarted#Query-with-a-stepper":{"type":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol","title":"Query with a stepper","abstract":[{"text":"Build a small notes store: open a database, create a schema, insert rows safely, run queries, and group writes in a transaction. By the end you will have a working command-line app that exercises the core LoomCore API.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/loomcore\/gettingstarted#Query-with-a-stepper","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/tutorials\/LoomCore\/GettingStarted#Query-with-a-stepper","kind":"section"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/Database/Service":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Service","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Base class for cross-cutting database services that hook into transaction lifecycle events."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Service","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/database\/service","title":"Database.Service","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Database\/Service","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"ex-02-schema.swift":{"content":["import Foundation","import LoomCore","","extension Database {","    static func openTaskTracker(at url: URL) async throws -> Database {","        let db = try await Database.open(url: url)","","        try await db.setJournalMode(.wal)","        try await db.setSynchronous(.normal)","        try await db.setForeignKeys(true)","","        try await db.exec(","            \"\"\"","            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS categories (","              id BLOB PRIMARY KEY,","              name TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE","            )","            \"\"\"","        )","        try await db.exec(","            \"\"\"","            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tasks (","              id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,","              category_id BLOB NOT NULL REFERENCES categories(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,","              title TEXT NOT NULL,","              completed_at REAL,","              metadata TEXT","            )","            \"\"\"","        )","","        return db","    }","}"],"fileType":"swift","identifier":"ex-02-schema.swift","syntax":"swift","highlights":[{"line":12},{"line":13},{"line":14},{"line":15},{"line":16},{"line":17},{"line":18},{"line":19},{"line":20},{"line":21},{"line":22},{"line":23},{"line":24},{"line":25},{"line":26},{"line":27},{"line":28},{"line":29},{"line":30},{"line":31}],"type":"file","fileName":"Database+Setup.swift"},"doc://LoomCore/tutorials/LoomCore":{"abstract":[{"text":"Walkthroughs that build small but realistic apps end-to-end. Start with the beginner tutorial to learn the core API; the advanced tutorial covers expression-based queries, custom types, and transaction lifecycle hooks.","type":"text"}],"tit